 ## Overview
-FineSplat is a feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting framework that predicts a set of 3D Gaussians from $N$ context views using a two-stage dual-grouping strategy to balance local detail preservation with global multi-view reasoning [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [YoNoSplat](16425-yonosplat.md) and [ZipSplat](16425-zipsplat.md) by employing high-resolution 4x4 patch tokens instead of coarser 14x14 patches, combined with serialized attention for 3D spatial grouping to avoid the prohibitive cost of global multi-view attention [S1, unofficial].
+FineSplat is a feed-forward 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) framework that predicts a set of 3D Gaussians from $N$ context views (with or without known poses) using a two-stage dual-grouping strategy to balance local detail preservation with global multi-view reasoning [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes itself from sibling methods like [SparSplat](15813-sparsplat.md) and [Generalizable Pixel-Wise 3D Gaussian Splatting](17059-generalizable-pixel-wise-3d-gaussian-splatting.md) by employing high-resolution $4 \times 4$ patch tokens and serialized 3D spatial attention, avoiding the prohibitive cost of global multi-view attention while preserving fine-grained visual information [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-FineSplat operates in two stages: view-wise token grouping (Stage 1) and 3D spatial token grouping (Stage 2) [S1, unofficial].
+**Inputs and Outputs:**
+*   **Input:** $N$ context views (images $I \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times H \times W \times 3}$) and their camera poses (intrinsics and extrinsics). Poses may be known or predicted.
+*   **Output:** A set of 3D Gaussian primitives (centers, covariances, colors, opacities) representing the scene.
 
-### Inputs and Outputs
-*   **Inputs:** $N$ context RGB images $I \in \mathbb{R}^{N \times H \times W \times 3}$ and their corresponding camera poses (intrinsics and extrinsics) [S1, unofficial]. Training samples $N$ from $\{6, 12, 24, 32\}$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Outputs:** A set of 3D Gaussian primitives $\mathcal{G} = \{\mu, \Sigma, \alpha, c\}$, where $\mu$ is the mean, $\Sigma$ is the covariance (defined by scale and rotation), $\alpha$ is opacity, and $c$ is color [S1, unofficial].
+**Data Structures:**
+*   **Tokens:** A set of $M$ fine-grained tokens $z \in \mathbb{R}^{M \times d}$, where $M = N \cdot (H/p) \cdot (W/p)$ and $p=4$ is the patch size.
+*   **Gaussians:** $K$ Gaussian primitives predicted per token.
 
